{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 1"},"body":"The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.\n\nInspected: Read variance_main, ℓ_k(n)=log(en) for k=3 and 1 for k≥4, and U_k=log 2/−log(1−2^−k).\n\nCapture rebinding by Codex, 26 October 2026: the Atlas capture revision changed after an outside-report wording correction. The pinned Lean text, configuration, paper text and proposed relation are unchanged; no new review is implied.","content_sha256":"sha256:c7443750ce90afdc7d48ab39439dde214a96ad6f77b0991040f433a15d42f1d5","fingerprint":"sha256:fb40b4cf741a54a0e9749522412d3aceff778d687fed64d37728a952bcd00ec4","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:8f93bd2b1d89a67b7c19ed9e52d713820344eaa8db1e7d811ed63437bc5b6f3a","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.RandomKSAT.variance_main"],"explanation":"For every k≥3, both statements give the n·ℓ_k(n) upper bound and a positive linear lower bound for the random k-SAT hitting-time variance, including the stated capped variants. The cap parameter requirements agree: arbitrary positive B for the upper bound and B>U_k for the lower bound.","fingerprint":"sha256:1c2da6320f33c61fab4ad5d424aeff018da12b820bafeb4c535ebda7e936a60c","limitations":"A lower-bound lemma covers o